[]{#s:hetTdual label="s:hetTdual"}

The analysis of T-duality in the type IIA frame of CHL models can be repeated without essential modifications to describe T-duality in the heterotic frame (equivalently, S-duality in the type IIA frame). Under a change in the moduli $$T_{\text{het}}\to -\frac{1}{NT_{\text{het}}}\ ,\qquad U_{\text{het}}\to -\frac{1}{NU_{\text{het}}}\ , \qquad S_{\text{het}}\to S_{\text{het}}\ ,$$the heterotic CHL model is mapped to another four dimensional $\mathcal{N}=4$ string model.

